<description>
Crop each foreground sprite to its bounding box and pack the crops tightly along the sprites' layout axis.

Input structure:
- The input is a background grid containing multiple separated, monochrome, 8-connected sprites.
- The sprites all have the same bounding-box shape.
- The sprite centers are spread more in either rows or columns, defining a vertical or horizontal layout.

Rule:
- Extract each sprite's bbox crop.
- If the sprite centers span more columns than rows, order sprites left-to-right and concatenate the crops horizontally.
- Otherwise, order sprites top-to-bottom and concatenate the crops vertically.

Key insight:
- The output is not a recoloring; it is the same sprites with all empty space between their bboxes removed.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "8-connected monochrome foreground sprites s with equal bbox shape, ordered along the larger spread axis",
  "dst": "tightly packed output slots d in the same horizontal or vertical order",
  "match_cond": "rank(s left-to-right for horizontal layouts, or top-to-bottom for vertical layouts) == rank(d)",
  "transform": "crop each s to its bbox and paste the crops unchanged with all inter-sprite background spacing removed",
  "grid_shape": "one sprite bbox tall by N bbox widths for horizontal layouts, or N bbox heights by one sprite bbox wide for vertical layouts"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-18 rows x 10-18 cols, background 0
  sprites:
    count: 2-4, each monochrome with distinct non-zero color
    bbox: 3x3 (all sprites share identical bbox shape)
    pattern: same binary pattern across all sprites [observed], 4-7 filled cells, 8-connected single component
    symmetry: LR and UD symmetric [observed]
  layout:
    axis: horizontal (col_span > row_span) or vertical (row_span > col_span)
    dominant_span: >=5 (center-to-center distance along layout axis)
    cross_span: <=4 (center-to-center distance along cross axis)
    constraint: no bbox overlap along layout axis; unique start coordinates along layout axis
    min_gap_on_layout_axis: >=0 cells between consecutive bboxes
  placement:
    margins: >=1 cell from all grid edges to any sprite bbox
    sprites scattered irregularly (non-uniform gaps along both axes)
  output:
    horizontal layout -> 3 rows x (3*N) cols, sprites ordered left-to-right by col position
    vertical layout -> (3*N) rows x 3 cols, sprites ordered top-to-bottom by row position
    crops concatenated with zero gap

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose N in [2,4], pick N distinct non-zero colors
    2. Generate a 3x3 binary pattern (4-7 cells, 8-connected, LR+UD symmetric)
    3. Build output by concatenating N copies of the pattern (each colored differently) along chosen axis
    4. Choose layout axis (H or V); set grid dimensions large enough to scatter N 3x3 bboxes with >=1 margin and varying gaps
    5. Place bboxes along layout axis with non-overlapping positions and random offsets on cross axis (cross_span < dominant_span)
    6. Paste each colored sprite crop at its assigned position on the background grid to form the input
```
