<description>
Move each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color
  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.
- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly
  one side of the cross.

Rule:
- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object
  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.
- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.
- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.

Key insight:
The marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,
and only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "each 8-connected composite object made of a 4-pixel blue marker sprite attached to a 5-pixel colored cross",
  "path": "straight away from the marker sprite until the composite bbox reaches the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "move the whole composite rigidly along that path",
  "transform": "rotate the 3x3 colored cross 180 degrees within the composite; keep the marker sprite unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 5-18 rows x 5-18 cols, background 8 (azure)
  objects:
    count: 1-4 composite objects, each 9 foreground pixels
    marker_color: single color shared by all markers; most frequent fg color, pixel count = 4 * object_count; always 1 (blue) [observed]
    structure: each object bbox is 3x6 (horizontal) or 6x3 (vertical)
    marker_block: |
      fixed 4-pixel shape in one 3x3 half, rotated per direction:
        left:  1..|.11|1..   right: ..1|11.|..1
        top:   1.1|.1.|.1.   bottom: .1.|.1.|1.1
    cross_block: 5-pixel plus/cross in the other 3x3 half; center always 4 (yellow); 4 arm colors all distinct, none = bg or marker
  placement:
    objects 8-connected-separated from each other in input
    distance from object bbox to target edge >= 2 [observed]
    objects sharing same target edge must occupy non-overlapping row/col bands (no collision after move)
  rule:
    move_direction: away from marker side to opposite grid edge (left->right, right->left, top->bottom, bottom->top)
    cross_rotation: rotate 3x3 cross block 180 degrees within the composite
    marker_block: unchanged
    final_position: object bbox flush against target grid edge, same row (horizontal) or column (vertical)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid H x W (5-18 each), object count N (1-4), and marker color (use 1).
    2. For each object, pick direction (left/right/top/bottom) and assign a row/col band at the target edge for the output. Ensure non-overlapping 3-row (horizontal) or 3-col (vertical) bands at each edge.
    3. Build each output object at its target-edge position: construct a random 5-color cross (center=4, arms from remaining non-bg non-marker colors), attach the direction-appropriate marker block.
    4. Derive input by inverting the transformation: rotate the cross block 180 degrees back, then place the composite at a random interior position along its movement axis (>= 2 cells from target edge). Verify no overlap with other input objects.
```
